## 7. APPLICATION FIELDS REQUIRED PANEL (Screen B)

Do not reuse the full `AdminApplicationFieldsPanel` UI as-is — that component (from FE-06) includes a catalog dropdown, category filters, and preset buttons meant for *initial configuration during drive creation*. Screen B is a simpler **post-creation toggle view**: a flat list of field names, each with a single on/off switch, plus one "Save Configuration" button at the bottom.

Build a new, smaller component: `features/drives/components/central-drive-fields-toggle.tsx`
- Reuse the same 21-field catalog data source (`application-fields-catalog.ts`) so field names/keys stay consistent everywhere in the app
- Render each field as a row: label + toggle (use the same toggle/switch primitive used elsewhere, e.g. shadcn `Switch` if already installed, otherwise match the visual style of existing toggles in the codebase)
- Local state for toggles, "Save Configuration" button calls `updateCentralDriveApplicationFields(driveId, fields)`, disabled while pending (`useTransition`), toast on success/failure
- Do not include the "required" (red asterisk) styling logic beyond what's already stored per field — just reflect existing `isRequired` flags visually (as shown in the screenshot, several fields are marked with a red label, e.g. Full Name, Roll Number, Current CGPA, Resume, Active Backlogs, Phone Number) and let toggles control `isEnabled`, not `isRequired`, in this panel. Changing which fields are *required* vs merely *enabled* is out of scope for this toggle panel.

